## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time ingestion basics, per-tenant routing, idempotence, and basic observability on GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming sources; Dataflow (Python) transforms
- BigQuery per-tenant tables with environmental isolation
- Idempotence via insertId; dead-letter queue handling
- Basic monitoring and dashboards for latency/cost

## Code Example
```javascript
class ValidateAndRoute {
  process(element) {
    const data = JSON.parse(element);
    if (!data.tenant_id || !data.timestamp || data.value == null) return;
    return [{ tenant: data.tenant_id, value: data.value }];
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test DLQ routing and failed-event replay?
- What metrics would you surface in a simple dashboard to catch data skew or lag?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a production-grade multi-tenant pipeline with strict data isolation, governance, and cost controls across GCP services, plus a robust testing and rollback strategy.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation with per-tenant Cloud Storage and per-tenant BigQuery datasets
- Dataflow pipeline correctness, idempotence, and scheduling
- IAM and IAM Conditions for least privilege
- Cross-region DR, data residency, and backup strategy
- Cost visibility with labels and budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
class ValidateAndEnrich {
  process(element) {
    if (!valid_schema(element)) return;
    const enriched = enrich(element);
    return enriched;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema changes across tenants without downtime?
- How do you enforce per-tenant security boundaries in a shared data lake?

